<!-- @after 6. Deep Dive: Force-Update + Soft-Deprecation Flow (15 min) :: animation -->
### Step through the version-policy gate

<figure class="stepper" data-illustrated><span class="stepper-title">Version policy at app start</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="3"><div class="node" data-el="app" data-art="phone" data-art-role="client"><strong>Installed app</strong><small data-text="appV">version 4.9.2</small></div><div class="node" data-el="api" data-art="server" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>Policy endpoint</strong><small data-text="apiV">GET /v1/app/policy</small></div><div class="node" data-el="cache" data-art="database" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Cached policy</strong><small data-text="cacheV">none yet</small></div></div><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="2"><div class="node" data-el="gate" data-art="gate" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>AppPolicyGate</strong><small data-text="gateV">waiting</small></div><div class="node" data-el="screen" data-art="screen" data-art-role="client"><strong>What the user sees</strong><small data-text="screenV">splash</small></div></div><div class="node is-key" data-el="event" data-art="signal" data-art-role="runtime"><strong>What happens</strong><small data-text="eventV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
  {
    "label": "App starts",
    "caption": "Version 4.9.2 asks the policy endpoint for the current rules and sends its version in the X-App-Version header.",
    "add": ["app", "api", "cache", "gate", "screen", "event"],
    "state": {"app": "active", "api": "active"},
    "text": {"eventV": "GET /v1/app/policy · X-App-Version: 4.9.2"},
    "handoff": {"from": "app", "to": "api", "kind": "page", "label": "version"}
  },
  {
    "label": "Policy arrives",
    "caption": "The server answers bannerBelow 4.10 and forceUpdateBelow 4.8. The app caches the policy for launches when the endpoint is unreachable.",
    "state": {"api": "done", "cache": "done"},
    "text": {"cacheV": "bannerBelow 4.10 · forceUpdateBelow 4.8", "eventV": "policy cached"},
    "handoff": {"from": "api", "to": "cache", "kind": "rows", "label": "policy"}
  },
  {
    "label": "Gate decides",
    "caption": "4.9.2 is not below 4.8, so there is no force update. It is below 4.10, so the status is DEPRECATED.",
    "state": {"gate": "active"},
    "text": {"gateV": "DEPRECATED", "eventV": "4.9.2 < 4.10, ≥ 4.8"}
  },
  {
    "label": "Soft path",
    "caption": "The user sees the deprecation banner above the normal content and keeps working. The app logs deprecation_banner_shown, so the team can watch update uptake.",
    "state": {"gate": "done", "screen": "warn"},
    "text": {"screenV": "banner + full app", "eventV": "deprecation_banner_shown"}
  },
  {
    "label": "Older install",
    "caption": "On another device, version 4.7.0 is below 4.8. The gate returns FORCE_UPDATE and shows only the update screen; its button opens the Play Store. The app logs force_update_shown.",
    "state": {"app": "warn", "gate": "active", "screen": "error"},
    "text": {"appV": "version 4.7.0", "gateV": "FORCE_UPDATE", "screenV": "update screen only", "eventV": "force_update_shown"}
  },
  {
    "label": "Endpoint down",
    "caption": "If the policy call fails, the gate uses the last cached policy. On a first launch with no cache, it falls back to OK rather than locking the user out because of a network problem.",
    "state": {"api": "error", "cache": "done", "gate": "done", "app": "active", "screen": "done"},
    "text": {"apiV": "unreachable", "gateV": "cached policy, or OK", "screenV": "app usable", "eventV": "never lock out on a network error"}
  }
]</script><figcaption>Two thresholds, read from the server and cached on the device, decide between the full app, a banner and a forced update. A missing policy never blocks the user.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after 12. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- **App, wire and schema versions move independently,** and installed clients cannot be forced to upgrade on the server's schedule.
- **Wire changes are additive.** Rename or retype by adding a field, deprecate the old one, and retire it only when usage data says so.
- **Every Room version bump ships a tested migration;** `fallbackToDestructiveMigration` never runs in production.
- **Two thresholds drive the gate:** a soft banner below one version, a forced update below an older one, both from a cached server policy.
- **Deprecate in stages:** headers (`Deprecation`, `Sunset`), banners, release notes, then force-update only for security, legal or unkeepable contracts.
- **Retire by data, not the calendar:** watch active installs and endpoint traffic per version before removing an old contract.
